WEBVTT

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.890
Fuurin

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.890
Fuurin

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.890
Tsujidou

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:03.890
Tsujidou

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.890
A handicap?

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.710
<i>So they think they can beat us even
when we start with a ten-run lead?</i>

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.030
Play ball!

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.110
<i>We'll make them regret doing that.</i>

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:19.450
<i>Not only will we stop them winning,
we'll beat them by eleven runs!</i>

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:26.480
All right!

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:31.190
Out!

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.550
Nice, Yayoi!

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.930
Nice double play!

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.140
Yay.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.600
This time it's a hit!

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:50.520
Too bad!

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.700
Three outs!

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.630
What?!

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.290
Nice, Chisato!

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.950
Yes!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.910
Fuurin

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.910
Fuurin

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.910
Tsujidou

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:58.910
Tsujidou

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:58.910
<i>I see.</i>

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.120
<i>Looks like playing them 
wasn't a complete mistake.</i>

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:07.800
<i>Chisato's one thing...</i>

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:11.010
<i>But </i>all<i> of these guys are really good!</i>

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.020
Fuurin

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.020
Fuurin

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.020
Tsujidou

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:47.020
Tsujidou

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.180
<i>Top of the second.</i>

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.810
<b>You Disappoint Me!</b>

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.020
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.520
<i>We seriously didn't score
a single run in the first?</i>

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:53.310
<i>I'm not too worried about their pitcher,</i>

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.120
<i>but their defense is a lot 
better than I expected.</i>

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.660
<i>Looks like we need to focus a little.</i>

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:07.910
Fair!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.240
Awesome!

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.500
Nice batting!

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.710
Yay, a double!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.960
Seriously?

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.670
<i>He hit Oka's slider like it was child's play.</i>

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:21.070
<i>Did he anticipate it?</i>

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:25.350
<i>Batting fifth, first base, Kabashima-san.</i>

00:03:25.350 --> 00:03:27.310
Keep us rolling, Anita!

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:33.850
Foul!

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:35.860
<i>So that's it.</i>

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.570
<i>She tried to hit the first slider too.</i>

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:42.530
<i>I guess after the strikeouts last inning,
they're only swinging at sliders.</i>

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.110
<i>In that case...</i>

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:46.240
<i>we'll just switch to fastballs!</i>

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.670
What?!

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:00.050
Keep going!

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:02.720
Uh, what?

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.020
It's a home run.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.720
We have a house rule that any ball 
that hits the fence is a home run.

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:10.730
All right!

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:12.810
We pulled two runs ahead on our own!

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.670
A girl... hit it all the way to the fence...

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.270
Nice!

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:19.980
Good job!

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.450
Hey now... They're scoring before
we've even overturned their handicap.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.430
What happened, Inoue?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:28.280
I threw a fastball like you signaled,
and she hit it sweet!

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:30.060
M-My bad.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.500
I thought she was waiting for a slider...

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.230
What's going on?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:38.990
<i>Batting sixth, right field, Nishina-kun.</i>

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.190
We're not done yet!

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:43.130
Let's keep it goin'!

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.050
Ball!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.020
<i>I don't get it. They're not picking
just one type of pitch to swing at?</i>

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.000
Nice!

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.280
Good eye, good eye!

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:55.450
Hit it, Nishina!

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.400
Just getting flustered won't
get you closer to him, Chiyo.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.890
You have to yell: "Go, Nishina-kyun!"

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.360
Be quiet, you!

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.270
Foul!

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:14.560
You got this, you got this!

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:16.000
You can do it!

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:22.670
<i>You're something else, Daigo.</i>

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:27.120
<i>It only took you one inning of watching
from the bench to figure out their pitching.</i>

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:32.600
Their secret weapon is a fast slider
that's almost as quick as a fastball.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:36.940
We were sitting ducks in the first inning
because that slider messed us up.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:41.050
But this pitcher has a tell 
when he throws a slider.

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:45.040
It's pretty common among pitchers 
when they first learn the slider.

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.940
They focus so much on making it curve,

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:49.550
they can't help releasing
lower than for a fastball.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:56.210
Once you know that, you can pick which pitch
you swing at: the sliders or the fastballs.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:00.170
Just pick whichever one works 
for you and swing at them!

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:02.900
He hit it!

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.030
Sweet!

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.340
We're not stopping!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.300
<i>What the hell is this team?</i>

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.010
Nice hit.

00:06:11.010 --> 00:06:12.760
You got that slider good.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.130
Of course I did.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.030
Don't lump me in with
your lame strikeout trio.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:22.770
You only hit it because of
Daigo's advice, you little brat!

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:26.350
I'm gonna twist your nose off
and stuff it down your throat!

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:28.900
He got a hit, but he's still in trouble.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.880
<i>Batting seventh, pitcher, Sakura-san.</i>

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:35.830
<i>We've scored two runs,
and we're piling on the pressure.</i>

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.580
<i>Swinging free risks a double play,
but our weaker batters are up next.</i>

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:40.290
<i>Let's just go for a hit.</i>

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:41.600
Play!

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.000
<i>Damn! What's going on here?!</i>

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:49.420
<i>This inning, they're hitting my fastballs
and my sliders like they're nothing!</i>

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.350
<i>If he releases high, it's a fastball.</i>

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.970
<i>If he releases low, it's a slider.</i>

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:58.850
Ball.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.290
Nice!

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.110
That's good, Senpai!

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:03.690
Good eye, good eye!

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:08.530
<i>Nope! I can't tell what's coming at all!</i>

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.470
Strike!

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:17.950
<i>I guess his arm did move
a little differently that time.</i>

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.980
<i>I should see it clearly after
a couple more times at bat.</i>

00:07:20.980 --> 00:07:24.420
<i>I can't believe Daigo and the others 
could read it on their first time up!</i>

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.210
Ball!

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:30.510
Strike!

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:31.970
<i>Wait...</i>

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.430
<i>I think I see it now!</i>

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:42.630
Out!

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:48.890
Well, seeing a pitch and hitting it
are two different things, you know.

00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.740
That was pretty okay.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.280
Nearly in the sweet spot...

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:56.240
<i>Batting eighth, third base, Kandori-san.</i>

00:07:56.850 --> 00:07:58.330
You're out!

00:07:58.630 --> 00:08:02.620
<i>Batting ninth, left field, Fujii Chiyo-san.</i>

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:03.130
Two outs after gettin' a runner.
That's the bottom of the order for ya.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.760
Hey, Chiyo...

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.760
It's your turn to bat. You're up now.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:11.880
Huh?

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.720
Yeah... Okay...

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.460
What's going on?

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:22.390
She looked white as a ghost. Is she okay?

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:24.960
No, I think she's totally not okay...

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:28.570
We basically only did
defense drills yesterday.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:31.360
Well, just having her at the plate is enough.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.520
I don't expect her to get a hit.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:34.320
Play!

00:08:35.070 --> 00:08:36.660
<i>What's up with this girl?</i>

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:39.390
<i>Her legs are literally shaking.</i>

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:42.660
<i>Her stance and grip make her
look like a complete beginner.</i>

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:45.290
Chiyo, you got this!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.130
Yeah, I don't think so.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.010
Strike!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.520
Oh, wow.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:56.720
Well, I guess it's kinda scary at first.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:02.870
<i>She's watching.</i>

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:09.170
<i>Chisato's watching me be 
pathetic and laughing at me.</i>

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:13.400
<i>I knew it. I should've refused to play.</i>

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:20.160
<i>I quit baseball because 
I had zero talent for it.</i>

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.120
<i>So how could I ever hit these pitches?!</i>

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:26.140
Strike two!

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:29.630
<i>It was too cruel.</i>

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:35.590
<i>I was born first and got
my glove and my bat first.</i>

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:38.800
<i>But my little sister 
surpassed me in an instant.</i>

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:46.020
<i>Even as a child, I could sense Dad
shifting his focus onto Chisato.</i>

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:54.610
<i>That's right. That's why I quit.</i>

00:09:55.210 --> 00:09:58.320
<i>So what am I even doing here?</i>

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.280
The heck? She ain't gonna hit it
standin' that far from the plate.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:05.200
Ball.

00:10:05.480 --> 00:10:08.450
<i>It doesn't matter.
I'm just here to fill the roster.</i>

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:10.170
<i>This is enough.</i>

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:14.760
<i>I'd look even more pathetic
if I actually tried doing something.</i>

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.680
<i>You know... I should just abandon the game...</i>

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:22.770
<i>...like I did back then.</i>

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.360
Chiyo!

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:31.050
You <i>know</i> there's no way
you'll hit anything standing there!

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:32.190
Is this a joke to you?

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.460
I saw you last night!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.320
You were doing practice swings!

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:40.780
Why'd you even do them, then?

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:45.790
It made me happy when I saw you 
taking baseball seriously again,

00:10:45.790 --> 00:10:47.250
so what is this?!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.690
Even if you're only making up the numbers,

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:53.090
I can't believe you'd actually 
treat baseball like a joke!

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.460
You disappoint me!

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:56.330
It's embarrassing!

00:10:57.590 --> 00:10:58.650
<i>Chisato...</i>

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.680
Chiyo, the game is still live!

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.720
Stop chatting in the middle of a game!

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:07.680
Ball!

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.890
Two balls, two strikes.

00:11:24.790 --> 00:11:25.330
What?

00:11:29.030 --> 00:11:29.670
Foul!

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:31.460
Unlucky. A whisker away.

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:33.690
No freakin' way. She hit it!

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.920
That was super close!

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.170
You can hit this!

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:39.910
Close call. That came outta nowhere.

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:41.630
Don't be careless, Oka!

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:50.180
<i>I finally got a good pitch to aim at,
but I couldn't make it count.</i>

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.780
Shigeno-senpai, please call a timeout.

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.650
T-Timeout!

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.650
Chiyo, you didn't listen to
his advice earlier, did you?

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:04.310
About that pitcher's tell.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:06.400
Um, no...

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:11.040
Anyway, even if I had, it wouldn't 
do a klutz like me any good.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.840
That's just not true!

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:17.490
I never thought you were as
unathletic as you said you were!

00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:21.590
I also don't get why you quit baseball
when you could've gotten so good at it!

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:25.070
You just have too little faith in yourself!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.440
Hey, you're taking too long!

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.980
U-Uh, right! Sorry!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:37.250
Chiyo, take these.

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:41.710
It's better if you wear these batting gloves.

00:12:41.710 --> 00:12:44.060
I've got another pair.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:46.030
Thank you.

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.670
Well?

00:12:50.670 --> 00:12:52.950
I told her about the pitcher's tell,

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.880
but it's not like a beginner
 can handle a slider,

00:12:56.880 --> 00:12:59.860
so I told her to just swing
as hard as she can at the fastballs.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.630
But I doubt they'll throw
another fastball now.

00:13:05.030 --> 00:13:06.960
<i>Her form...</i>

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:12.740
Ball!

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:14.350
Three and two!

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:15.970
Did ya see that?

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:18.310
She read it after one bit of advice?!

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:21.530
Nah, doubt it. She just couldn't swing.

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:23.540
Nice one, Chiyo!

00:13:23.540 --> 00:13:24.490
Good eye!

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:29.120
I never thought you were as
unathletic as you said you were!

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.700
You just have too little faith in yourself!

00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:35.410
<i>Those were all just lies.</i>

00:13:38.310 --> 00:13:40.240
<i>Trying to butter me up...</i>

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:45.050
<i>I won't let you sweet-talk me
 into playing baseball again</i>

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.760
<i>just because you're short on players!</i>

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.830
Second!

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:56.300
Heck yeah!

00:13:56.300 --> 00:13:57.730
He missed the catch!

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.290
No way...

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:02.650
She hit it? Whoa.

00:14:02.870 --> 00:14:05.610
We went from two outs to another big chance!

00:14:06.250 --> 00:14:07.870
Anita. Kan-chan.

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.460
Relieve the base coaches.

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:10.850
Okay.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.270
See? What did I say?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.790
You think an "unathletic person"
can hit a slider without training?

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:19.420
Sounds more like a genius to me.

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:26.090
<i>Batting first, center field, Fujii Chisato-san.</i>

00:14:26.340 --> 00:14:27.140
<i>Dammit.</i>

00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:28.300
<i>What's going on here?</i>

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:30.120
Ball!

00:14:31.170 --> 00:14:33.080
He's no good.

00:14:34.460 --> 00:14:35.880
Hey, Mario.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:38.560
Mario!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.610
Get ready.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.450
Warm up your arm, Mario.

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:01.630
Yes!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:06.090
Fuurin

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:06.090
Fuurin

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:06.090
Tsujidou

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:06.090
Tsujidou

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:04.450
Yes, 13 runs!

00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.090
Well, it's three, really.

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:13.860
No phones on the bench.
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:15.510
Oh, my bad.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:20.310
I was just reviewing my form
in the previous game.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:23.810
I don't want to pitch
'cause I'm done for the day.

00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:27.400
<i>So he </i>did<i> hear me. He was just ignoring me.</i>

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.860
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:38.290
Oh, huh. We gave up three runs, somehow.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:43.030
Oka's no good to us in his current state.
Go pitch before the game gets away from us.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.920
But that wasn't the plan.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.210
Y'know, Coach, if I bust
my arm, you'll get fired.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:51.870
You only pitched one inning!

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:53.180
Just get out there!

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:54.840
Ball!

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:56.090
Ball four!

00:15:56.090 --> 00:15:58.140
Boring.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.060
All right!

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.060
Bases loaded!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.850
Oh man, talk about pressure...

00:16:03.380 --> 00:16:06.240
Dammit. What the hell is going on here?!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.820
Nothing's working. That's just how it is.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.310
Mario?

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:19.870
Timeout!

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:22.140
What's this?

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:24.960
Their battery took a timeout 
and now they're takin' another?

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:32.600
They're taking years. Stop wasting time.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:34.930
We were on a roll!

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.750
They're buying time for
the pitcher in the bullpen.

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:39.390
They'll probably switch pitchers now.

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.120
We're switching pitchers.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:42.100
Mario!

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.660
H-He's huge!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.740
He seems special in that unique uniform.

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:06.370
Thanks for buying me some time.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.240
Um, I'm sorry, Mario.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:10.670
You were done for the day,
 but because I'm having an off-day...

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:13.630
It's rough with bases loaded,
but please get us out of it.

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.370
An off-day?

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.460
That's how good Oka is on a <i>good</i> day.

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:21.860
He still hasn't realized that?

00:17:21.860 --> 00:17:23.310
Hey! He's your senior!

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:27.520
He probably got his ass handed
to him 'cause his tell is so obvious.

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:29.570
His control's all over the place,

00:17:29.570 --> 00:17:32.360
which is why he's on the B-Team
even though he's a second-year.

00:17:32.850 --> 00:17:35.820
And Inoue-san, please make
sure you catch my miracle balls.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:41.790
You're a second-year who also yo-yos between the B-Team and A-Team.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:45.960
A southpaw, huh?

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:48.890
His pitches look pretty fast.

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:51.500
You think he's their ace?

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:52.670
Probably.

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.140
What a stupid look,
giving us a ten-run handicap,

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.380
then panicking and putting in their ace.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:58.800
Play!

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:06.270
<i>This team's basically all girls.</i>

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:09.310
<i>People who mess up against this team...</i>

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.190
<i>...should just quit baseball!</i>

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:17.740
Ouchy, that really hurt!

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.700
Hit by pitch!

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.740
Sweet! A forced run!

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:26.430
14 runs!

00:18:27.960 --> 00:18:29.330
Hey, kid.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:32.110
Were you checking out my butt
when you threw that?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.750
Wha— No, I wasn't!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:37.470
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:40.180
<i>It's hard to tell because it hit Sawa-san,</i>

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:44.660
<i>but the fact she couldn't dodge it
in time means it must've been fast.</i>

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.890
Man, my butt hurts.

00:18:47.830 --> 00:18:50.880
<i>I need to hit before he sorts out his control.</i>

00:18:57.660 --> 00:19:00.570
I have no interest in guys' asses.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:05.080
Oh, and by the way, I'm just getting warmed up.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:12.710
Strike two!

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:15.420
Wow, those are so fast.

00:19:15.650 --> 00:19:17.520
Wh-What <i>is</i> that?

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:19.880
I've never seen anything like it.

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.220
No wonder my butt still hurts.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:28.720
<i>Mario's a southpaw who can pitch
at 130 kmph with a rubber ball.</i>

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:33.460
<i>And he's only a first-year in middle school.
He's got frightening potential.</i>

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.980
<i>These kids won't even be able to graze it.</i>

00:19:38.210 --> 00:19:39.360
Foul!

00:19:42.140 --> 00:19:43.910
That's Dai-chan for ya.

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:04.710
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.510
<i>Don't insist on fastballs
just because he grazed it.</i>

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.810
<i>Not bad, short stuff.</i>

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:18.590
That's good, that's good!

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:20.190
Yer timin' is gettin' better!

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.660
<i>This guy's really pissing me off.</i>

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:27.670
<i>Getting cheered on by cuties
on a battlefield for men?</i>

00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:30.330
<i>I'm so damn jealous, you little brat!</i>

00:20:33.070 --> 00:20:34.080
Foul!

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:35.470
Inoue!

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:37.620
T-Timeout!

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.440
Hey, Mario, you need to listen 
and stop pitching fastballs.

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:45.130
Stop being so petty and
throw a breaking ball already.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.040
I'm not being petty.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.480
I'm just worried 'cause the bases are loaded.

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:55.560
I mean, you might let my 
Mario-balls go past you, y'know?

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.540
D-Don't look down on me!

00:20:57.540 --> 00:21:00.280
Of course I'll catch them!
Just trust me and throw them!

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:01.930
Hm, if you say so...

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.740
Don't look at the ball! Look at me!

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:10.580
<i>So far, he's shaken off every sign 
and only pitched fastballs.</i>

00:21:10.910 --> 00:21:12.990
<i>He'll start throwing breaking balls now.</i>

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:14.320
Play.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.880
<i>Oh, fine then.</i>

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:20.880
<i>My arm's warmed up now,
so why don't I give you a taste?</i>

00:21:21.450 --> 00:21:22.340
<i>Of my...</i>

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:27.140
<i>...miracle Mario-balls!</i>

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:29.140
<i>A fastball!</i>

00:21:34.240 --> 00:21:35.370
<i>No, it's not!</i>

00:21:43.640 --> 00:21:45.150
Not an uncaught third strike!

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:47.610
That idiot! He let it past him after all!

00:21:48.040 --> 00:21:49.070
Whoosh!

00:21:49.070 --> 00:21:50.350
First!

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:52.550
Out!

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:56.210
That was impressive.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.670
Fuurin

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.670
Fuurin

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.670
Tsujidou

00:21:56.210 --> 00:22:00.670
Tsujidou

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.790
Three outs!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.910
Change sides!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:02.290
So about that...

00:22:02.290 --> 00:22:03.000
I-I'm sorry.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.130
I'll definitely get the next one.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:06.260
I'll stop it for sure.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.650
D-Didn't that one just
 suddenly change course?

00:22:09.650 --> 00:22:10.610
Yeah.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:13.180
What <i>was</i> that?

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:18.140
It came down like a forkball,
but went off at an angle like a slider.

00:22:19.080 --> 00:22:20.730
This is bad news.

00:22:21.320 --> 00:22:25.040
I doubt we'll be scoring any 
more runs against that pitcher.

00:22:25.930 --> 00:22:27.630
We need to bring our best defense!

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:02.700
I need to pitch to the end by myself.

00:24:03.080 --> 00:24:05.040
I'm Fuurin Middle's ace!

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:06.050
I don't believe it.

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:08.550
We've been playing their B-Team up to now?!

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.300
Fuurin

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.300
Fuurin

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.300
Tsujidou

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:09.300
Tsujidou

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:11.840
So what kind of baseball
does their regular team play?

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:15.070
This is what our region's 
best players look like?

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:16.800
They're too good for us!

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:18.160
We're not going to give up.

00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:20.180
There's got to be <i>some</i> way for us to win.

00:24:20.180 --> 00:24:24.980
<b>A Storm Brewing</b>

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:22.720
Next time: "A Storm Brewing!"

00:24:22.720 --> 00:24:24.750
Run to the stage of your dreams!
